A||||6||dennis_6||Please help - I need to get started before it gets cold||||1||
Z||000000||dennis_6||11-11-2001||06:12 PM||||I have two 86 Fiero SE's.  I am giving one to my father.  I got a parts car that is identical to my 86 SE except it has a four speed and the body is in poor condition.  I want to end up with a four speed under the good body.  Should I try to swap the cradles and tranny parts or should I just swap all body panels and interior items.  The parts car is pretty beat up and I am sure it holds hidden nightmares.  What should I do?  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||maryjane||11-11-2001||07:26 PM||||I had plenty of trouble with putting the eng/trans/cradle back in (4cyl '84 auto)(my own fault for not marking stuff well enough), but when you think of all those fasteners on the body panels, plus the interior, I would go with the power train swap. I'm not much help on this really, but this will bump it up to the top.||||reg||1
Z||000002||avengador1||11-11-2001||07:40 PM||||Since you will have to take both cradles out you might as well put the best engine and transmission together, and while you're at it put in a new clutch and throw out bearing. It's a lot easier to replace anything that needs to be replaced while the cradle is out. This will ensure less problems down the road.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||11-11-2001||08:00 PM||||Drop the cradles is probably the way to do it...<P>As mentioned above put a new clutch in. also replace the clutch arm pivot bushings.<P>Replace the cradle bushings while it's out and easy to get at.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||artherd||11-11-2001||08:07 PM||||Definately swap the cradles...<P>If you haven't done it before some simple tools (and a strong friend or six!) will make it MUCH easier.<P>Engine hoist ($150) and build a creepy-crawlie rooling thing to rool the droped cradles around with.<P>Lose the cradle, let it sit on the rooling thing. then lift the car (seems to be the perfered method.)<P><BR>PS: didja get the distributor I sent yet? Let me know, sorry it took so dam long!<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000005||dennis_6||11-11-2001||08:46 PM||||Ben - I ordered the heads.||||reg||1
Z||000006||dennis_6||11-12-2001||02:47 PM||||Thanks everyone for replying.  I guess I will swap cradles and stuff then.  Does anyone know of a webpage for convering an auto car to a manual?  Thanks again.||||reg||1
